WEBVTT

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:12.080
Hey, there's one!

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.060
There's another!

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.200
Meteor showers are cool, huh?

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:17.990
Yeah.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.800
Hey. My big sister said that

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.570
if you make a wish three times 
before a shooting star disappears,

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:30.120
it'll come true.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.910
Isn't that just superstition?

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.160
You think so?

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.660
But my sister really believes it.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.260
What did you say?

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.390
That's so childish.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:48.160
But I am a child.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.980
I thought you didn't believe it, Kin-chan.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.370
Just thought I'd try.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.370
What did you wish for?

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.340
I wished for...

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.460
Kusatsu-san.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.750
So this is where you were.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.830
What are you doing here with all the lights out?

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.270
Looking at the stars.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.010
Stars?

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.970
Yes. Shooting stars.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.440
Shooting stars? Wishing on a star, eh?

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.340
I didn't know you were such a romantic, Kinshiro.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:24.280
So, what did you wish for?

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.620
I wished for...

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.030
World domination, of course.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:06.920
Cute Little Boys of Love and Youth

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.980
Woosh, woosh, woosh!

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.380
S-Stop it! Stop it, stop it!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.850
But you stink.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.860
What's it called? Animal stink?

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.380
But washing me like this...

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.970
When you stink,

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.800
after I cuddle you, people tell me <i>I</i> stink!

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.740
I don't stink! You're the ones who—

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.910
Huh? We're the ones who stink?

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:34.910
What kind of stink?

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:36.720
Human...

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:37.800
Human stink?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:38.560
Yes!

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.250
Oh, really?

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:42.570
Do wombats have a sharp sense of smell?

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:47.220
I just happen to resemble your Earth animal.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:50.420
I am not an actual wombat!

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:51.820
Then what are you?

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.490
I am wfirocbx...

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:54.460
Wfiro...?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:58.130
Xjudsu...

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.100
Huh? Ikuju...

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.420
Oh, whatever! Let's just go with Wom-san!

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:04.930
Don't run away!

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:05.970
Made it!

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.450
Give it a break already, Yumoto.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.360
You're just like a child.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.480
Well, in Yumoto's case, 
it's not just his behavior.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:17.940
He looks like a kid, too.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.250
What's wrong with that? 
That means I look young, right?

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.040
Young? You've got to be kidding.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:25.610
We're in high school, you little kid.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.160
Please stop calling me a kid.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.410
Okay, Yumoto-kun, 
what's your dream for the future?

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.340
To be a superhero!

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.080
See? A kid.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.150
Hey, everyone! There's a kid in here!

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.930
Besides, we're already superheroes.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.350
Though we didn't ask to be...

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:43.300
Oh, that's right.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.770
Well, I will be taking my leave ahead of you.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.950
Hey, I'm not done yet.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:51.950
Pardon.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:56.030
You're not just young. 
You really are a child, Yumoto.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:59.800
Do you still pay the 
child fare to ride the bus?

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:05.490
I'm so jealous. You don't 
have to spend as much money.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.550
You got me, huh?

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.230
Just kidding!

00:05:08.890 --> 00:05:11.580
That's the kind of thing 
that makes you a kid.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.210
Anyway, you need more than 
just youth on your side.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.500
You need to channel that into appeal.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.930
If you ask me, I'd say you're 
pretty childish yourself, Ryuu.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.890
Oh, Yufuin-senpai, you don't know my true power.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.640
What true power?

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.910
From married women to 
elementary school girls—

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.860
You can't beat me in video games!

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.680
You be quiet!

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.610
Okay...

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.250
If we were in the samurai ages,

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:45.590
we would have had our coming of age 
ceremony and be full-fledged adults by now.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:47.830
Your looks don't determine 
whether you're actually young.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.750
That's a senior for you. You're so mature.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.170
Senior?

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:56.750
Well, senior can refer to an 
older person or an upperclassman.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:58.720
That's right, Senior-senpai.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:02.260
I feel like he just called me an old man.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.660
Does my face really look that old?

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.430
It means that your appearance 
and behavior are both mature.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.830
Being called mature is a compliment, right?

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:13.950
That's why, in the samurai ages, 
they'd shave off their forelocks

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:15.520
and make themselves intentionally bald.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:21.040
*This is his individual opinion about forelock-shaving.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.070
Oh? Was that artificial baldness?

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:21.040
Yes, they thought being bald 
made you look more adult.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:24.170
So if I shaved myself bald, 
people might not call me a kid?

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:27.060
No, it would just look like a miso commercial.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.520
What does that mean?

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.480
Does my face look old?

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.530
En-chan, are you really worried about that?

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:36.880
Maybe so... Does my face look old?

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.330
Being young is a wonderful thing!

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:42.790
Me too! Me too!

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:49.220
What is that?

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.340
You don't understand at all.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.810
My inner calm reflects itself on my face.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.240
He's so worried about it.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:14.530
I'm sorry, Mister. Were we being too loud?

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:18.970
Hey, Yumoto.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:20.630
He's not an older man.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.030
He wasn't wearing his uniform,

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.620
so I thought he was just some older guy, too.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:27.810
But I just now realized...

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:30.700
He's a student at our high school.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.690
They call him "the guy with 
the face of a 50-year-old."

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:39.180
<b>Igarao Oyaji</b>

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:39.180
Igarao Oyaji!

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.160
<i>Damn it. I'm not an old man.</i>

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:47.960
Sir, good morning.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.560
<i>When I go to school, 
they confuse me for a teacher.</i>

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:49.580
Go ahead!

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.370
<i>When I ride the train, 
people give up their seats for me.</i>

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.020
What's with that old guy?

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:55.000
<i>I didn't choose to be born 
with a face like this.</i>

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:59.350
I want to enjoy my youth like 
a high school student, too.

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:02.380
I'm not an old man. I'm not an old man.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.640
I'm not an old man!

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:10.010
He's our next target, eh?

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:13.850
I see. I feel powerful dark energy from him.

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:18.860
His age complex will likely create 
a powerful negative field.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.230
Then let us go.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:25.150
Conquest!

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.320
We are the rulers of this blue world...

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.280
Caerula Adamas!

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:35.460
Now, release the Zundar Needle!

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:37.750
Donum!

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:03.020
Good morning, Gora!

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.760
Oh, you're up early, Yumoto.

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:06.430
Yeah, I've got club stuff.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:10.440
You do club stuff? Morning training?

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.150
Morning cuddles!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.310
Morning <i>cuddles</i>?

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:14.650
Yeah, morning cuddles.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.410
Thanks for the lunch, as usual!

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.530
Sorry it's rice balls again.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:22.910
Nah, your rice balls are 
the best in the world!

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.060
Woosh, woosh, woosh!

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:39.050
How long are you going to do that?

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.480
I can't believe you don't get tired of it.

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:42.130
But it's fun.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.440
Why not put that effort into a part-time job?

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.850
You could make a lot of money.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.830
That's not fun.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.550
Why not pick up girls?

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:52.980
No interest in that.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.360
Does my face really look that old?

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:57.950
Hey, are you still stuck on that, En-chan?

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:01.400
But that was the first time in my life 
I've been told my face looks old.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:05.250
People had only described me 
as "hot" or "gorgeous" before.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.710
I've never heard that...

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.100
Isn't that normal for an 18-year-old boy?

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:13.170
Isn't it people like Yumoto and 
Ryuu who are the exception?

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.460
Don't lump me in with Yumoto.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.890
I'm cute! He's a kid.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:19.430
You called?

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.330
No, no. That's not true.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.220
Having a face that looks old
is like, for example,

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:30.260
the husband in that anime who has 
a coworker with really prominent lips,

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.530
but it turns out he's really 27.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:36.470
Why are you talking about a nationally 
famous anime all of a sudden?

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:40.200
Why are you associating me, 
an 18-year-old, with that character who's 27?

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:43.130
Well, um, um...

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:45.930
The savior of the century's end 
with seven stars on his chest,

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:49.140
the cynical #2 of the Science Ninja Team,

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:50.950
and the protagonist's dark-skinned friend

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.840
voiced by Iizuka Shouzou
in that robot war story

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.400
are all 18, too.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:56.220
But you look much younger than them!

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:59.880
Why is this turning into even 
more of an anime superfan discussion?

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:03.430
And why is Iizuka Shouzou-san 
the only person you named outright?

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.420
What are they talking about?

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:06.520
No idea.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:09.400
I like unagi more than anago!

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.730
Now's my chance!

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:16.610
Hey, wait!

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:38.010
<b>Zaou Ryuu
Born March 13th
Blood Type B / Pisces
Hobby: Snowboarding
Likes: Girls, cherries</b>

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:40.210
<b>Earth Defense Club                       (lol)</b>

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.210
Woosh, woosh, woosh!

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:42.560
Woosh! Woosh, woosh!

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.980
Stop it, Yumoto! What are you doing?

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:47.450
Well, Wom-san ran away, so...

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.760
Cut it out! Why me, then?

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:50.990
He really is a kid.

00:11:50.990 --> 00:11:54.900
Such an unproductive endeavor 
won't earn you a single yen, you know.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.280
There's nothing fun about 
two men fooling around.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.440
Woosh! Woosh, woosh!

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.200
What is this?

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:05.820
I'm getting an irresistible urge to tickle En-chan.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.750
Woosh, woosh, woosh!

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.350
Why you now?

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:14.210
Well, it just looked so fun! Woosh, woosh!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:16.710
Senpai, what are you doing?

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.480
Actually, I want to do it, too!

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:22.140
Woosh, woosh, woosh!

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.520
What are you doing, Io?

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.500
Damn! I'm getting revenge!

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:27.950
Then I'll get revenge, too!

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:30.360
Turning the tables is no fair!

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.230
Hey, doesn't something seem weird?

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.190
Like what?

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:43.860
Now that you mention it, why are we 
acting like elementary schoolers?

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.500
I just got the urge to do it.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.830
It's almost like we've turned 
into elementary schoolers.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.540
Yeah, 'cause we <i>have </i>turned 
into elementary schoolers!

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:55.010
What's going on here?!

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.650
Terrible news! An enemy's appeared!

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.140
Wh-What's all this?

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:11.080
What's going on?

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:14.140
The students have all become children.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:16.230
Darn it! I had a date after this!

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.340
<i>That's</i> what bothers you?

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:20.620
Yay! Yay! This is kinda fun!

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:23.050
He's the only one who doesn't 
seem to have changed much.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:24.080
Yeah.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:27.490
You think this is the 
work of an enemy monster?

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:29.420
Hey! Look at that!

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:41.600
Become young again! Become young again!

00:13:44.190 --> 00:13:47.160
Is that monster's power 
turning everyone into children?

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.360
Everyone! Time for Love Making!

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.210
Right!

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:52.170
Love Making!

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:56.180
The Sparkling Prince!

00:13:56.180 --> 00:13:57.690
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:13:58.320 --> 00:13:59.780
The Flashing Prince!

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:01.230
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:02.960
The Piercing Prince!

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.690
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:06.580
The Roaring Prince!

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:08.150
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.160
The Thrilling Prince!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.590
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:13.830
We are...

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:16.030
Wait, what's up with this?!

00:14:16.030 --> 00:14:19.470
That's weird. Why's it so baggy?

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:22.000
Our other clothes changed to child sizes.

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:24.880
This setup is lacking consistency.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:28.500
And I really liked my costume, too.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.180
You like that thing?

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:33.980
Who are you people?

00:14:34.580 --> 00:14:36.690
You, who befoul our beloved Earth!

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:39.400
No justice can come from loveless power!

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:41.600
Love is all!

00:14:41.600 --> 00:14:43.570
Live for love! Die for love!

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:46.610
We are the heirs to the throne of love!

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:49.490
Battle Lovers!

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.300
Feel the power...

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:53.970
Of love!

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.380
You monster! We're gonna fight you!

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:01.880
Battle Lovers? We'll see about that.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.040
What was that?

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:04.350
Take this!

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:06.130
Scarlet Lumiere!

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:10.840
Huh? Why?

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:14.080
Has our power been halved 
because we're children?

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.810
It's the child rate?

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:19.430
Then allow me to take the lead.

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.750
What's wrong, Battle Lovers?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.930
These baggy clothes are hard to move in.

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:43.930
Damn.

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.570
I hate looking so uncool.

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:47.970
<i>That's</i> what bothers you?

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:50.880
How unsightly.

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:52.800
Damn it...

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:55.610
Fall to ruin, Battle Lovers!

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:05.020
Hey, all we're doing is saying "wah!"

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:08.490
Fall to ruin! Fall to ruin, all of you!

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:12.290
This is your punishment for treating me 
like an old man based on the way I look!

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:14.110
What did he say?

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:15.610
Is it possible he's...

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:17.580
"The guy with the face of a 50-year old"...

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.000
Igarao Oyaji!

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:22.430
Don't call me by that nickname!

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:32.180
Then I'll make you even younger.

00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:44.080
What's going on?

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:45.280
I can't move!

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:49.280
It appears we've turned into 
kindergarteners this time.

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:50.240
What was that?

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:54.110
You literally can't raise a hand against me.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.860
Darn you, darn you, darn you.

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:59.210
Oh, it undid our transformation.

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:02.950
Undid? Or disrobed?

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:06.550
"Disrobed our transformation" 
doesn't sound right for the genre.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.240
This is very embarrassing.

00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:12.970
I'm not embarrassed, but I won't 
forgive you for making <i>that</i> smaller.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.440
At this stage, you're effectively babies.

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:19.340
No, you <i>are</i> babies.

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:23.440
Then I'll send you to hell, 
as easy as taking candy from a baby!

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:29.600
Damn... At this rate...

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:30.610
Are we done for?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:36.820
If I'd known this was going to happen, 
I would have spent all my savings.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.280
The women of the world will lament this.

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.210
Wait a minute.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.320
What is it at a time like this?

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:49.860
Something's weird.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:50.950
Weird?

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:54.920
The setup here is that everyone's turning 
young because of him, right?

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.590
That's right. So?

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.260
Then it really is weird.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:00.260
<i>What's</i> weird?

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:03.600
Well, if that's the old man high school student,

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.520
he wouldn't look like that, 
even if he turned young.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:11.450
I get it. Even young, 
someone who's ugly is still ugly.

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:14.200
He'd never become a pretty young boy.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:15.700
Which means this is...

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:17.330
An illusion!

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:18.740
Oh, no!

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:21.410
Now!

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:34.590
Love Attack!

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:39.480
What?!

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:54.720
You're not really an old man.

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:57.040
You're an 18-year-old high school student.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:19:02.490
Isn't it the resentment you feel that's
really turning you into an old man?

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:07.210
That all sounds impressive,
but it's not really fixing anything.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:11.580
Love Shower!

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:19.240
What is this strange sensation?

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:21.010
Comfort... healing...

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:24.010
I see... So this is love.

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:31.090
Love is over!

00:19:31.090 --> 00:19:32.780
We're back to normal!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:41.290
Well, let's all put this 
behind us and have a bath!

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.660
We're naked anyway!

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:44.740
Speaking of which, where'd our clothes go?

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:46.160
Let's go!

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:51.010
Accursed Battle Lovers.

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:52.760
They foiled us yet again.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:56.900
It appears we failed once more.

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:59.420
Lord Zundar, I am sorry.

00:19:59.790 --> 00:20:01.630
No matter.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:05.380
Let them bask in their overconfidence for now.

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.730
Next time, I swear...

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:09.670
I'll be counting on you.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:10.400
Sir.

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:15.220
But I thought this plan to turn the enemy 
into elementary schoolers to seal their power

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:17.310
would work out well.

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:20.410
Elementary schoolers, huh?

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:22.770
Is something wrong?

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:24.400
No... It's nothing.

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:28.960
Just remembering something from long ago.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:36.130
Woosh, woosh, woosh!

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:38.200
Enough of that, Yumoto.

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:39.760
He really is a kid.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:44.950
Well, he's the only one who didn't change 
at all when the enemy made us young.

00:20:44.950 --> 00:20:48.720
No matter how young you 
make the kid, a kid is still a kid.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.090
Oh, no!

00:20:53.090 --> 00:20:56.270
Don't worry. The shield function made 
it so he wouldn't recognize our faces.

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:57.240
Oh, that's right.

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:04.670
You seem to be in a good mood.

00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:06.580
Did something good happen to you?

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:11.040
Well, actually, I got a girlfriend.

00:21:13.090 --> 00:21:14.890
Oh, does she like older men?

00:21:14.890 --> 00:21:15.450
Hey!

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:17.520
That's right.

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:20.870
She says they're wonderfully reliable.

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:26.480
She said she made a wish on 
a star to meet a wonderful man.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:30.210
I see...

00:21:30.210 --> 00:21:31.290
You heard him.

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:32.880
Why are you telling me that?

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:35.980
I'm glad to hear it, 
though it's also kind of annoying.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:38.060
Yes!

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:40.410
What is it?

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:44.460
He reminded me that I made a wish
on a shooting star when I was little.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:45.350
What was it?

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:47.350
To be a superhero.

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:49.120
Just like a kid.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.150
Well, I was a kid.

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:53.050
You can't say anything about Yumoto.

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:55.730
That reminds me.

00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:59.060
What did he wish for then, I wonder?

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:01.460
Woosh! Woosh, woosh!

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:05.380
Please stop...

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:09.970
Ma-Ma-Macho...

00:23:40.740 --> 00:23:44.890
For some reason, the Press Society guys 
are hanging around the Defense Club.

00:23:44.890 --> 00:23:48.270
They muscle in on my calls to girls. 
It's beyond annoying!

00:23:48.270 --> 00:23:50.620
Remote control? I'll buy you one of those!

00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:52.830
Next time: To Steal Love Without Regret.

00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:54.610
Next Time

00:23:50.620 --> 00:23:54.610
To Steal Love Without Regret

00:23:52.830 --> 00:23:54.330
Love Making!
